From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:41:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] Declare URLSession's data task publisher at Apple's
 level, from iOS 7

URLSession.swift declared URLSession.dataTaskPublisher(for:) and
URLSession.DataTaskPublisher inside the OCombine namespace, which the
module no longer has, and on every release, while URLSession is iOS 7
API, so the module did not compile for an iOS 6 deployment target with
availability checking on. That implementation is removed, and
URLSession+DataTaskPublisher.swift declares the publisher on URLSession
itself, marked iOS 7, which is where the SDK's URLSession is. On iOS 6
the class comes from the backports a port carries.

The publisher creates the data task when the subscriber first asks for a
value, sends the task's one result (the data and the response, or the
error as a URLError) and finishes; cancelling it cancels the task. A
response with no data is sent as an empty body, and a completion with
neither a response nor an error is reported as badServerResponse.
